-- Review of the 2026-10-30/31 research inbox (PRs #330-#336 and older): Greensboro NC, Rockville MD, Troy NY and Newport RI.
-- Greensboro: Temple Emanuel's class page says "You MUST purchase a 2026 Mah Jongg card from the National Mah Jongg League prior to class"; Sparrow and Dragon's own site says "complimentary 2026 National MahJongg League Card" and "An introduction to American Mahjong". Both pages were read directly (open-play dates 11/18, 12/2, 12/16 and the November calendar were checked on the live pages). Sparrow and Dragon's Summerfield sessions are filed under Greensboro because the calendar says "Greensboro or Summerfield". The sold-out Fall Mahjong League and the invitation-only private beginner classes are not listed.
-- Rockville: Mahj Over Matter's own site says "American Mahjong Events in Bethesda, Chevy Chase & Rockville, MD" (Mosaic Cuisine, Rockville; Lao Sze Chuan, North Bethesda; the private Mahj Room boot camp is left out). Quince Orchard Library's event pages say "We play American Mah Jongg according to National Mah Jongg League rules" (Monday sessions 11/9-12/14 read on the library site; the branch is in Gaithersburg, Montgomery County). Bender JCC's course page (quote as returned by three research runs; the site blocks our fetch with a 403) names American Mah Jongg and the NMJL card; the Monday beginner series is listed, the full Tuesday PM series is not.
-- Troy and Newport: no organiser's own page states American or NMJL (Meetup group at a possible private home; a hotel listing seen only as a search snippet; a magazine mention), so those stay NEEDS_REVIEW in new unpublished cities.
