-- Greensboro (2 clubs + 7 sessions) and Rockville (3 clubs + 9 sessions) now have five or more active rows: published with intros.
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Greensboro''s American mahjong centres on a synagogue and a locally run lessons-and-events group. Temple Emanuel hosts open play on the first and third Wednesday evenings of each month, and Sparrow and Dragon offers beginner classes, strategy classes and guided open plays, most of them at Martin''s Mercantile in nearby Summerfield, with occasional pop-ups at a mall department store or a restaurant. Bring the current National Mah Jongg League card, since classes and tables are built around it. Beginners are well served: Sparrow and Dragon''s introductory class provides every card and set, so you only need to show up.' WHERE "slug" = 'greensboro';
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Rockville''s American mahjong is spread across a community centre, a restaurant circuit and a county library. Bender JCC runs multi-week courses for adults at several levels, Mahj Over Matter hosts social open play and beginner mini-lessons at restaurants in Rockville and North Bethesda, and the Quince Orchard branch of the Montgomery County library hosts free drop-in play on Monday afternoons. These groups play American mahjong, so bring the current National Mah Jongg League card. If you are brand new, start with a Bender JCC beginner series or a Mahj 101 mini-lesson before joining open play.' WHERE "slug" = 'rockville';
